{
  "requirement": "TBV exposes configuration for its supplied Bedrock, OpenAI, and Ollama\nagents. The configuration selects a backend and carries its model, connection,\ncredential-selection, and model-option settings.\n\n```rust,ignore\n#[non_exhaustive]\npub enum AgentConfig {\n    Bedrock(BedrockConfig),\n    OpenAi(OpenAiConfig),\n    Ollama(OllamaConfig),\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl<D: Domain> AgentSettings<D> for AgentConfig;\nimpl Clone for AgentConfig;\nimpl Debug for AgentConfig;\nimpl<'de> Deserialize<'de> for AgentConfig;\nimpl PartialEq for AgentConfig;\nimpl Serialize for AgentConfig;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "Subject obligations: `AgentConfig` has Bedrock, OpenAi and Ollama variants carrying backend settings. It is `#[non_exhaustive]` and implements `AgentSettings<D>`, `Clone`, `Debug`, `Deserialize`, `PartialEq` and `Serialize`. The `agent_config.serialization` and `agent_config.settings` children refine it. Their detail is reviewed under those requirements, not here.\n\nCoverage:\n- **Variants and settings, Serialize/Deserialize:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/config.rs#mod[tests]/fn[all_backends_preserve_nested_settings_and_credentials]` deserializes a full JSON object for each of the three backends. Each selects its variant through the `backend` tag. It asserts that re-serializing yields the identical JSON, so model, connection, credential-selection and nested option settings are preserved. It also round-trips through a string.\n- **PartialEq:** the same test asserts `config == copy` after the round trip.\n- **Using each variant's settings:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/providers.rs#mod[tests]/fn[supported_backend_settings_create_transports_without_sending_requests]` builds providers from the OpenAI, Ollama and Bedrock configs. It checks that the output limits derived from the options match.\n- **AgentSettings<D>:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[configured_agents_initialize_only_when_asked_and_report_setup_errors]` passes an `AgentConfig` to `ValidationCache::with_agent`. That only compiles because the impl exists, and the test asserts the config's credential-selection setting takes effect in the resulting error. `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` covers the public export.\n- **Defaults and credential resolution:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/config.rs#mod[tests]/fn[option_defaults_and_credential_resolution_are_deterministic]` covers the defaults and credential selection.\n- **Clone, Debug, PartialEq, non_exhaustive:** `AgentConfig` derives `Clone`, `Debug` and `PartialEq`. The derives contain no conditionals or transformations of their own, so no separate test is required. `#[non_exhaustive]` and the empty `AgentSettings<D>` impl are compile-time properties.\n\nI found no untested obligation and no wrong expected result.",
